$ signet sandbox doctor --help
-- stdout --
Check whether the sandbox can run against your networks, and why not.

Prints the CLI's and the simulator's versions, the simulator's lanes (the
ledger protocols it runs, and the host each links), the live protocol of the
selected network (and testnet), with a verdict for each, the stellar, cargo
and Docker (for --localnet) versions, and the fork cache's size.

A network the simulator has no lane for is never run on the wrong host: the
verdict says whether the network is ahead of the simulator (upgrade
@signet/cli), behind it (an older release has its lane), or in a gap. Exits
11 when a checked network has no lane, 3 when there is no simulator.

Usage:
  signet sandbox doctor [flags]

Examples:
  signet sandbox doctor
  signet sandbox doctor --network mainnet --rpc-url https://mainnet.example/rpc --json

Flags:
  -h, --help                        help for doctor
      --network-passphrase string   passphrase of a custom --network
      --rpc-url string              the RPC to read the selected network's protocol from

Global Flags:
      --context string         deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --drift string           when an entry fetched for the fork changed on-chain after the fork ledger: warn, fail (exit 6), or refork (pin the latest ledger and run once more) (default "warn")
      --insecure               allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                   write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string         Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --sign-with-key string   identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string          identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string             Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)
-- stderr --
(empty)
-- exit 0 --
